{"id": "EUVD-2026-101234", "enisaUuid": "97c03721-0cc7-3fde-ae5a-b1444269048a", "description": "LibreCAD libdxfrw through LC2.2.0 (LibreCAD through 2.2.1.5) contains a stack-based out-of-bounds read vulnerability in dwgReader18::readFileHeader() caused by calling strlen on non-NUL-terminated buffers. Attackers can supply a crafted AC1018, AC1024 or AC1027 DWG file without NUL bytes in the decrypted header to read adjacent stack memory and crash the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:07:40", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/LibreCAD/LibreCAD/issues/2554", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libdxfrw-dwg-header-oob-read", "https://github.com/LibreCAD/libdxfrw/blob/LC2.2.0/src/intern/dwgreader18.cpp#L248", "https://github.com/LibreCAD/LibreCAD/blob/v2.2.1.5/libraries/libdxfrw/src/intern/dwgreader18.cpp#L248", "https://github.com/LibreCAD/libdxfrw/commit/0c5595930b20917a40ed7c188475eaca624b8ce9", "https://github.com/LibreCAD/LibreCAD/commit/abd1f4a8e32dbd871c986086227502217200cd4b", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/librecad-libdxfrw-through-lc2-2.0-stack-out-of-bounds-read-via-dwgreader18-readfileheader"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v4r9-37cv-99h9", "CVE-2026-110606"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05aa3f09-70d9-3113-ac32-87e240b19067", "product": {"name": "libdxfrw", "vendor": {"name": "LibreCAD"}}, "product_version": "0 \u2264LC2.2.0"}, {"id": "626d5a3b-874e-3e05-9ccc-01565cfdfcec", "product": {"name": "LibreCAD", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.2.1.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "32a6c2ad-b919-3cff-b4f8-683bc6cabe5b", "vendor": {"name": "LibreCAD"}}], "isExploited": false}